## pptxgenjs patterns

Preferred library: `pptxgenjs`. Fallback: `python-pptx`.

**Slide size: 7.5 × 5.625 in (4:3).**

```js
pres.layout = 'LAYOUT_4x3';   // or define a custom one
pres.defineLayout({ name: 'CUSTOM', width: 7.5, height: 5.625 });
pres.layout = 'CUSTOM';
```

**Color tokens** (use these exact values, don't improvise):

```js
const COLOR = {
  bg: 'FFFFFF',
  text: '000000',
  muted: '999999',
  caption: '666666',
  boxLight: 'F5F5F5',
  boxBlue: 'F2F6F9',
  boxWarm: 'FAF9F6',
  border: 'CCCCCC',
  teal: '028090',     // accent
  patternRed: 'C0392B', // pattern-break breadcrumb only
};
```

**Reusable helpers:**

```js
function addSlideNumber(slide, n) {
  slide.addText(String(n), {
    x: 0.18, y: 0.13, w: 0.4, h: 0.25,
    fontFace: 'Arial', fontSize: 9, color: COLOR.muted,
  });
}

function addBreadcrumb(slide, text, isPatternBreak = false) {
  slide.addText(text, {
    x: 0.55, y: 0.13, w: 6.7, h: 0.25,
    fontFace: 'Arial', fontSize: 9, bold: true,
    color: isPatternBreak ? COLOR.patternRed : COLOR.teal,
  });
}

function addCollabReminder(slide) {
  slide.addText('Think first. Discuss with a partner. Then write.', {
    x: 0.4, y: 5.33, w: 6.7, h: 0.25,
    fontFace: 'Arial', fontSize: 9, color: COLOR.caption,
  });
}

function addQuestionBox(slide, text, { x, y, w, h, fill = COLOR.boxLight }) {
  slide.addShape('roundRect', {
    x, y, w, h, fill: { color: fill },
    line: { color: COLOR.border, width: 0.75 },
    rectRadius: 0.05,
  });
  slide.addText(text, {
    x: x + 0.15, y: y + 0.08, w: w - 0.3, h: h - 0.16,
    fontFace: 'Arial', fontSize: 12, color: COLOR.text,
    valign: 'middle', lineSpacingMultiple: 1.15,
  });
}

// 3-Tier Concept Question — the load-bearing layout
function addTierBlock(slide, label, prompt, y) {
  slide.addText(label, {
    x: 0.55, y, w: 2.0, h: 0.25,
    fontFace: 'Arial', fontSize: 10, bold: true, color: COLOR.text,
  });
  slide.addText(prompt, {
    x: 0.35, y: y + 0.26, w: 6.8, h: 0.55,
    fontFace: 'Arial', fontSize: 10, color: COLOR.text,
    lineSpacingMultiple: 1.15,
  });
}
```

**Image placement** for Contrast Set (side-by-side, when using images instead of text):

```js
// Left image — fits within 7.5 in slide width
slide.addImage({ path: leftImgPath, x: 0.4, y: 0.85, w: 3.2, h: 2.5, rounding: true });
slide.addText(leftLabel, { x: 0.4, y: 3.4, w: 3.2, h: 0.25, fontSize: 9, color: COLOR.caption, align: 'center' });

// Right image
slide.addImage({ path: rightImgPath, x: 3.9, y: 0.85, w: 3.2, h: 2.5, rounding: true });
slide.addText(rightLabel, { x: 3.9, y: 3.4, w: 3.2, h: 0.25, fontSize: 9, color: COLOR.caption, align: 'center' });
```

## Inserting into an existing deck

pptxgenjs builds new decks, not insertions into existing ones. For inserting into an existing .pptx, use **python-pptx** with direct XML manipulation via `lxml` to reorder slides (python-pptx doesn't support slide reordering natively). The pattern:

1. Open the existing deck with `python-pptx`
2. Build the new insert slide(s) using the layouts above
3. Reorder via XML: access `presentation.part.package.presentation_part.element` and move the new `sldId` elements to the desired positions in the `sldIdLst`
4. Save

If Katherine only wants the insert slides as a standalone deck she'll drag in manually, skip the reorder step and just build a clean deck with pptxgenjs — it's faster and cleaner.

## Visual QA pass

Before delivery:

1. Convert .pptx to PDF: `libreoffice --headless --convert-to pdf <deck>.pptx`
2. Convert PDF to JPEG thumbnails: `pdftoppm -jpeg <deck>.pdf thumb`
3. Scan every slide for: text overruns, questions that got truncated, missing writing space, duplicate questions (a content slide already had one), image sizing issues, font-size drift (nothing should drift below the calibrated minimums in the global rules — 8pt word bank label is the floor)
4. Fix and re-render if needed

## File naming

Deliver as `<Lesson Name> — Student Slides.pptx` in `/mnt/user-data/outputs/`, then call `present_files`.
